    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d615-a6">

                <pb facs="0930" n="802" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg802"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6 in No.
                    209.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Neuchâtel</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-03-06"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 6,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The department of police declares that in consequence of new information it has
                    received which is of a nature to invalidate the suspicion of which Dr. Emeis, of
                    American nationality, has been the object, the order of expulsion pronounced
                    against him has been revoked, so that he can freely sojourn in the canton of
                    Neuehâtel, provided he deposits his papers and takes a permit to sojourn.</p>
                <closer>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">seal</hi>.] <signed>CORNAZ.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
